Hi Haakon,

I need to "rescale" the variable multiplying it * 1000 to have a sd which makes sense and that is not the the prior sd. This is quite an odd behaviour and may show that INLA does not see number smaller than 10^-03 and that these numbers are considered as 0. Is this something known?

Below, the fixed part of a simple model before and after multiplying the variable * 1000:

inla(pa ~ 1 + tdist,family="binomial",Ntrials=daily_abundance,data=iso4m)

